Id: dns007w
Severity: WARN
Category: network
Check: check_dns
Fix: Remove the duplicated lines from /etc/hosts, keeping the intended one.
References: hosts(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A line in /etc/hosts appears twice. The resolver takes the first, so
a later copy never applies; planted ahead of the real one, it misleads
everything resolving the name, root's daemons among them. Duplicates
usually creep in when tooling appends what is already there.
